    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **James Wood** (76.39) headlines our lineup as the premier start, capitalizing on a favorable matchup against Mitch Keller. **Wood** benefits significantly from leading off, where his elite 0.418 xwOBA is maximized by the high-volume plate appearance environment, making him a cornerstone for runs and stolen base potential. We are also projecting high output from **Brice Turang** (72.10) and **Isaac Paredes** (71.63); both are locked into prime spots against favorable matchups with SP_xERAs near 4.70. **Seiya Suzuki** (63.91) remains a high-floor play, bolstered by an advantageous park factor and wind blowing out, while his matchup against Andre Pallante provides a rare combination of speed-friendly delivery and platoon upside.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the optimizer today was the benching of **Corbin Carroll** (52.85). While **Carroll** provides elite speed, he is currently being suppressed by a poor matchup against Kyle Harrison (2.97 xERA) and an unfavorable platoon split. The projection engine ultimately prioritized the consistency of **Max Muncy** (62.14) and **Henry Bolte** (58.94), who both face the vulnerable Tyler Phillips and benefit from 10% park-factor boosts. Elsewhere, **Jose Caballero** remains a tactical play despite the platoon dip; his ability to capitalize on base-running opportunities remains a high-leverage asset for our stolen base targets. We are monitoring **Travis Bazzana** closely on the bench, as his 38% rain risk and challenging L/L matchup against Anthony Kay kept his score below the threshold required to displace our current starters. All lineup positions remain subject to minor adjustments pending final official lineups.",
